# The element numbers of the inp file are not in ascending order: 12, 11, 10
# and 1 in the first *ELEMENT, and 2 in the second, which comes after the
# *SOLID SECTION of the first. With E = 1000 and nu = 0.3, the strip PSTRESS
# (length 4, plane stress) and the square PSTRAIN (length 1, plane strain) are
# each pulled by 1 at their right end, which moves by 4.0E-03 in PSTRESS and by
# 1.0E-03*(1 - nu^2) = 9.1E-04 in PSTRAIN.
!VERSION
 3
!SOLUTION, TYPE=STATIC
!BOUNDARY
 LEFT, 1, 1, 0.0
 BOTTOM, 2, 2, 0.0
!CLOAD
 RIGHT, 1, 0.5
!SOLVER, METHOD=CG, PRECOND=1, ITERLOG=NO, TIMELOG=NO
 10000, 1
 1.0e-10, 1.0, 0.0
!WRITE, RESULT
!END
